Hello,

Due to the merge window, it will be hard to get patches accepted into
staging in the short term.  If you have no staging patches that have been
validated by a developer, you should stay with that for a while.  However,
if you have several patches that have been posted to the mailing list and
have received positive feedback from a developer, then you can start to
try some examples for the tracepoint project.

The first step it to run make UT=1 to find opportunities.  In my
experience this can be quite slow, so you might want to focus on a
particular subsystem.  I don't know if there are any in the staging files
that Greg handles, so you may need to go outside of that.  For the
purposes of the application period, you should initially just send your
patches to the outreachy mailing list.  This means that they will not be
accepted, so to qualify for Outreachy you need to do some basic staging
patches first.  Tracepoint patches can be submitted to the maintainers
after the merge window closes and after they have been approved here.

Please add the emails of the tracepoint project mentors to your
tracepoint patches:

Steven Rostedt <rostedt@goodmis.org>
Julian Braha <julianbraha@gmail.com>

Steven has provided a detailed example of how to fix up tracepoints, which
is below.  Please read the whole thing in detail, as it is very helpful
and will ensure that you do things in the right way.  The configuration
file he refers to is attached to this message.

Steven points out that the issues can be complex.  If you get stuck, you
can either try to find a simpler case to start with or send messages to
the list.  It may also be useful to send a message to the list up front
about what you are working on, if it seems to be taking some time, so
others work on something else.

julia


Here's an example of what to do.

Using the attached config (one that I used for some testing for other
issues) the output of the build had:

warning: tracepoint 'guest_halt_poll_ns' is unused
warning: tracepoint 'pcie_ltssm_state_transition' is unused
warning: tracepoint 'scsi_zone_wp_update' is unused
warning: tracepoint 'scsi_prepare_zone_append' is unused

Let's take a look at the first one: guest_halt_poll_ns

$ git grep guest_halt_poll_ns

[ Ignoring documentation ]

drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:static unsigned int guest_halt_poll_ns __read_mostly = 200000;
drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:module_param(guest_halt_poll_ns, uint, 0644);
drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:   if (block_ns > dev->poll_limit_ns && block_ns <= guest_halt_poll_ns) {
drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:           if (val > guest_halt_poll_ns)
drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:                   val = guest_halt_poll_ns;
drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:           trace_guest_halt_poll_ns_grow(val, dev->poll_limit_ns);
drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:   } else if (block_ns > guest_halt_poll_ns &&
drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c:           trace_guest_halt_poll_ns_shrink(val, dev->poll_limit_ns);
include/trace/events/power.h:TRACE_EVENT(guest_halt_poll_ns,
include/trace/events/power.h:#define trace_guest_halt_poll_ns_grow(new, old) \
include/trace/events/power.h:   trace_guest_halt_poll_ns(true, new, old)
include/trace/events/power.h:#define trace_guest_halt_poll_ns_shrink(new, old) \
include/trace/events/power.h:   trace_guest_halt_poll_ns(false, new, old)

The "TRACE_EVENT(guest_halt_poll_ns," is the defining of the trace event.

in include/trace/events/power.h there is:

#define trace_guest_halt_poll_ns_grow(new, old) \
        trace_guest_halt_poll_ns(true, new, old)
#define trace_guest_halt_poll_ns_shrink(new, old) \
        trace_guest_halt_poll_ns(false, new, old)

And those are called in drivers/cpuidle/governors/haltpoll.c

The Makefile: drivers/cpuidle/governors/Makefile has:

obj-$(CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_HALTPOLL) += haltpoll.o

Which means that haltpoll.c is only complied when
CONFIG_CPU_IDLE_GOV_HALTPOLL is enabled. If you look at my attached config
file, you will see that that option is not enabled. Which means that event
should only be created when that option is available.

